  "nl_text": "The database schema \"rschema_0328\" is used to store information about a survey system. It consists of six tables: Administrator, Survey, Question, Option, Text_answer_record, and Choice_answer_record.\nThe Administrator table contains information about the users who have access to the survey system, including their account names, IDs, names, passwords, and phone numbers. The Administrator_ID column is the primary key.\nThe Survey table contains information about the surveys themselves, including their access restrictions, access rules, anonymity, background image URLs, descriptions, start and end times, survey statuses, survey titles, and survey logos. The Survey_ID column is the primary key.\nThe Question table contains information about the questions in the surveys, including their descriptions, display orders, display styles, evaluation scores, for evaluations, question IDs, question titles, question types, required statuses, and validation types. The Question_ID column is the primary key.\nThe Option table contains information about the options for each question, including their display orders, correct answer statuses, option IDs, option contents, and question IDs. The Option_ID column is the primary key.\nThe Text_answer_record table contains information about the answers given by respondents to text questions, including their answer contents, question IDs, respondent information, submission times, and answer IDs. The Answer_ID column is the primary key.\nThe Choice_answer_record table contains information about the answers given by respondents to choice questions, including their answer types, option IDs, respondent information, submission times, and answer IDs. The Answer_ID column is the primary key.\nThe foreign key constraints ensure that the data in the tables is consistent and accurate, and that the relationships between the tables are properly maintained. For example, the foreign key constraint in the Question table ensures that the Survey_ID column in the Question table references a valid Survey_ID in the Survey table. Similarly, the foreign key constraint in the Option table ensures that the Question_ID column in the Option table references a valid Question_ID in the Question table.",
  "gold_question": "This is an online survey system. For administrator management, the system maintains administrator information including name, phone number, account, and password. Administrators can register, log in to the system, create, edit, delete surveys, and view survey statistics. For survey management, the system supports creating surveys, setting survey title, description, access restrictions, start and end times, access rules (public or password-protected), survey status (created, in progress, ended), survey logo URL and background image URL, anonymity settings, etc. Surveys can be associated with multiple questions. For question management, the system supports creating different types of questions (single choice, multiple choice, text, text area), setting question title, description, required status, validation type, display order, display style, evaluation status, evaluation score, etc. Questions can be associated with multiple options. For option management, the system supports creating options for questions, setting option content, display order, correct answer status, etc. Options can be single or multiple choice type. For answer recording, the system records users' answers to single or multiple choice questions, including option ID, answer type, submission time, respondent information, and also records users' answers to text questions, including question ID, answer content, submission time, and respondent information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0328.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0328\nCREATE TABLE `Administrator` (\n  `Administrator_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Account_Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Phone_Number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Administrator_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Survey` (\n  `Survey_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Access_Restrictions` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Access_Rules` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Anonymity` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Background_Image_URL` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Start_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `End_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Survey_Status` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Survey_Title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Survey_Logo` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Survey_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Question` (\n  `Question_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Survey_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Display_Order` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Display_Style` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Evaluation_Score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `For_Evaluations` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Question_Title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Question_Type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `Required_Status` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Validation_Type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Question_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `question_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Survey_ID`) REFERENCES `Survey` (`Survey_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Option` (\n  `Option_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Question_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Display_Order` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Correct_Answer_Status` tinyint(1) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Option_Content` text NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Option_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `option_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Question_ID`) REFERENCES `Question` (`Question_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Text_answer_record` (\n  `Answer_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Question_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Respondent_Info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Answer_Content` text NOT NULL,\n  `Submission_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Answer_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `text_answer_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Question_ID`) REFERENCES `Question` (`Question_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Choice_answer_record` (\n  `Answer_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Option_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Respondent_Info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Answer_Type` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `Submission_Time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Answer_ID`),\n  CONSTRAINT `choice_answer_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Option_ID`) REFERENCES `Option` (`Option_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
